        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\Delta=k^2\\geq 0$, so there is at least one real root.",
          "worked": "Since $\\Delta=k^2$, it is zero when $k=0$ and positive otherwise. The quadratic therefore has one distinct real root when $k=0$ and two distinct real roots otherwise.",
